{"id":"chatcmpl-bc48122edb518bb2","object":"chat.completion","created":1788642346,"model":"qwen38flashnext","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"\n\n```sql\nSELECT\n  c.id,\n  c.name,\n  SUM(o.amount) AS total_order_value\nFROM customers c\nJOIN orders o ON o.customer_id = c.id\nGROUP BY c.id, c.name\nORDER BY total_order_value DESC\nLIMIT 3;\n```\n\nFor SQL Server:\n\n```sql\nSELECT TOP 3\n  c.id,\n  c.name,\n  SUM(o.amount) AS total_order_value\nFROM customers c\nJOIN orders o ON o.customer_id = c.id\nGROUP BY c.id, c.name\nORDER BY total_order_value DESC;\n```","refusal":null,"annotations":null,"audio":null,"function_call":null,"reasoning":"We need answer user: \"Write a SQL query that returns the top 3 customers by total order value from tables customers(id,name) and orders(id,customer_id,amount).\"\nNeed provide SQL. done. Need final concise but maybe include standard ANSI SQL with LIMIT/TOP variants. Need ensure top 3 by total order value. Query: SELECT c.id, c.name, SUM(o.amount) AS total_order_value FROM customers c JOIN orders o ON o.customer_id = c.id GROUP BY c.id, c.name ORDER BY total_order_value DESC LIMIT 3; Mention SQL Server uses TOP 3, Oracle ROWNUM/fetch first. Could also include tie handling? Maybe if want dense_rank? But top 3 likely limit 3. Need possibly handle customers with no orders? \"by total order value\" likely only orders. Could mention if include customers with zero orders use LEFT JOIN. Need answer. Ensure clear.\n"},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop","stop_reason":null,"token_ids":null,"routed_experts":null}],"service_tier":null,"system_fingerprint":"vllm-0.28.1rc1.dev446+g798544433-tp4-ep-72ccc4a5","usage":{"prompt_tokens":82,"total_tokens":401,"completion_tokens":319,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":189}},"prompt_logprobs":null,"prompt_token_ids":null,"prompt_text":null,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"metrics":null}